    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1179">

                <pb facs="0969" n="853" xml:id="pg853"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5258.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Vera Cruz to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-17T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1912—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Felix Diaz, rebel general, with less than 1,000 men, expects hourly attack by
                    Federals. Consuls named committee who called upon Diaz, requesting avoid
                    righting within city. He promised or would advise, if unavoidable, unless
                    surprised. Gunboats against Diaz, under command Azueta, threaten bombard
                    barracks located center city. This evening consuls requested me hold American
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi> await arrival next boat and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> be sent back here at once. Telegraph
                    communications interrupted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
